From: K2B_RetroArch
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: kickpi-k2b: pin the mmc numbering

The K2B enables two MMC hosts here: mmc0 (microSD) and mmc1 (SDIO Wi-Fi);
the eMMC slot (mmc2) is disabled by 0065. Without aliases, mmcblk numbers
follow probe order, so the SD card is not guaranteed to be mmcblk0. The
image's root=/dev/mmcblk0p1 and the /dev/mmcblk0p2 ROM mount depend on it.
With these aliases the SD card is always mmcblk0.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-kickpi-k2b.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-kickpi-k2b.dts
@@ -23,6 +23,8 @@
 		i2c2 = &i2c2;
 		i2c3 = &i2c3;
 		i2c4 = &i2c4;
+		mmc0 = &mmc0;
+		mmc1 = &mmc1;
 		serial0 = &uart0;
 		serial1 = &uart1;
 		serial2 = &uart2;
